=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ VIM @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt Vim @VERSION@ for OpenVMS
1 'NOTICE
=prompt Vim is Charityware under the Vim License; see [VIM.DOC]LICENSE.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VIM.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for Vim
    At system startup: to define VIM$ROOT, VIM and VIMRUNTIME at every boot,
    add this line to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VIM$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the commands, add this line to LOGIN.COM:
    $ @VIM$ROOT:[000000]VIM$SETUP.COM

PRODUCT REMOVE VIM removes the product and deassigns the logical names.
